    "updated_at": "2026-06-20T03:46:02Z",
    "body": "Some possible future plans for improving the traversal performance:\r\n\r\n### Shared BLAS\r\n\r\n- MultiMeshBVH: Build one unified BVH over the triangles of multiple geometries - adding a dedicated \"object index\" per triangle. Or a \"MixedBVH\" that supports any kind of primitive / leaf?\r\n- Objects with shared geometry do _not_ go in the shared BLAS. Nor do specially marked \"dynamic\" or \"skinned\" meshes.\r\n  - Alternatively objects with shared geometry _could_ be placed into a single, shared multi-mesh BVH to speed things up at the cost of higher BVH node memory usage. Since each triangle index will come with an associated id we can share the underlying geometry data.\r\n\r\n### Shared Data Model\r\n- Keep vertices in object space (don't bake to world space) - preserves instancing memory, normals stay object-space.\r\n- Build the unified BVH over world-space triangle bounds (transform at build time to compute bounds only).\r\n\r\n### Dynamic Adjustments\r\n- While moving: refit each frame\r\n- On settle: trigger a full rebuild to restore tree quality.\r\n\r\n### Build Performance\r\n\r\n- Eventually use full GPU-based BVH construction and refit.\r\n- Wide BVH (BVH4/BVH8) — separate traversal-efficiency win, deferred for now.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
