    "created_at": "2026-07-03T02:28:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-03T02:28:54Z",
    "body": "> Do we want to migrate all examples to webgpu only? I expect there will be a period of adoption of webgpu where webgl will still be relevant. Or is this a temporary change to enable faster development?\r\n\r\nFrom my perspective the WebGLPathTracer is legacy and won't be maintained or updated anymore. It's simply too brittle, slow, and inconsistent to maintain and that limits the practical use, as well. Looking forward to when the WebGPU path tracer is merged to main: we can keep the WebGLPathTracer around for a few releases but I anticipate deleting it entirely with a v0.1.0 release. If users want to keep using the WebGL version they can continue to use whatever the last release is that included it. I'm open to other opinions but my plan is to keep these examples WebGPU only from here and if we need to compare to the WebGL version for feature parity etc we can look at the main branch.",
